//! The TPS63802 buck-boost converter, Texas Instruments, in the 10-pin VSON-HR (DLA) package,
//! 2 x 3 mm, order code TPS63802DLAR: the U15 of ORBIT, which makes the 3.3 V rail from the
//! battery.
//!
//! The pin table was WRITTEN BY HAND from TI's datasheet "TPS63802 2-A, High-efficient, Low IQ
//! Buck-boost Converter in DFN Package" (literature number SLVSEU9D, November 2018, revised
//! January 2021, 38 pages, fetched on 2026-11-10 from
//! <https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps63802.pdf>): section 7, Figure 7-1 and Table 7-1
//! "Pin Functions" (printed page 4) for the pads, names and what each pin is. The datasheet is
//! copyrighted: the numbers and names are facts, the words and the arrangement here are ours.
//!
//! The kinds: `EN` and `MODE` are `input` (the table says neither may be left floating), `FB`
//! is `input`, `PG` is `output` (the table says "open-drain output"), `VIN`, `VOUT`, `GND` and
//! `AGND` are `power`, and the inductor's pins `L1` and `L2` are `passive`: the inductor is
//! between them and the part's own switches drive them.
//!
//! The only figure stated is the feedback regulation voltage `.vref`: 500 mV, with an accuracy
//! of -1 to +1 % in PWM mode (electrical characteristics, section 8.5, printed page 6), for the
//! feedback divider (`std::parts::regulator::FeedbackDivider`: `.divider.vref == .u.vref`). In
//! power save mode (`MODE` low) the datasheet gives no accuracy in that table, and the value is
//! the PWM one. Everything else is left out, so the part is a boundary of the design and the
//! checks that need a number are listed as not evaluated: the input range (1.3 V to 5.5 V, and
//! more than 1.8 V to start), the output range (1.8 V to 5.2 V), the current limits, the
//! quiescent current, the switching frequency, the recommended inductance (0.37 to 0.57 uH,
//! 0.47 uH nominal) and the input and output capacitance (section 8.3, page 5). No std generic
//! is a buck-boost converter (`Buck` is a step-down interface, and `LinearRegulator` is a
//! linear one), so the part provides none and has no `dc` statement: the analysis of a rail
//! stops at it.

/// The TPS63802 in the 10-pin DLA package. Pin names are the datasheet's; the pad numbers are
/// its pin numbers. There is no exposed pad: `GND` (pad 8) is the long pad in the middle of
/// the right-hand side of the land pattern. `.vref` is the voltage the feedback pin is held at.
part Tps63802 {
    .designator &= "U"

    pins "VSON-10(2x3)" {
        //  pin    kind     name    pads
        .en      input    "EN"    "1"
        .mode    input    "MODE"  "2"
        .agnd    power    "AGND"  "3"
        .fb      input    "FB"    "4"
        .pg      output   "PG"    "5"
        .vout    power    "VOUT"  "6"
        .l2      passive  "L2"    "7"
        .gnd     power    "GND"   "8"
        .l1      passive  "L1"    "9"
        .vin     power    "VIN"   "10"
    }

    /// The feedback regulation voltage, 500 mV +/- 1 % in PWM mode (page 6).
    .vref: Voltage
    .vref &= 0.5V +/- 1%

    .package: Package
    catalog tps63802 by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
